      'The 2008 crisis is the Rosetta Stone of global economics, it connects every concept: supply and demand (housing bubble), monetary policy (low rates created it, QE solved it), fiscal policy (stimulus), trade (global collapse), currencies (dollar safe haven), systemic risk (interconnected banks), regulation (failures that allowed it, reforms that followed), and international coordination (G20 response). If you understand 2008, you understand how the global economy works as a system. The key lesson: in a connected world, there are no isolated problems and no isolated solutions.'
