      1,
      'Correct! Wages are primarily set by supply and demand. Only ~1.5% of workers have elite coding skills, but tech companies desperately need them, low supply + high demand = high wages. About 3.7 million Americans are teachers, supply is larger relative to (mostly public sector) demand. The gap reflects market forces, not the "value" of the work to society.',
