        { term: 'Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC)', definition: 'A tax credit for low-to-moderate income workers that effectively tops up wages. The most effective U.S. anti-poverty program.', example: 'A single parent earning $25K receives ~$3,600 in EITC, a 14% wage boost that lifts many families above the poverty line.' }
