        'The economics of clean energy have transformed in the past 15 years. Solar costs dropped 95%, from $4/watt (2008) to $0.20/watt (2024). Wind dropped 70%. Battery storage dropped 90%. Solar is now the cheapest source of new electricity in most of the world, beating coal and gas on pure economics. This isn\'t because of subsidies, it\'s because of learning curves, scale, and technological improvement.',
