        { term: 'Levelized Cost of Energy (LCOE)', definition: 'The total lifecycle cost of generating electricity from a source, allowing apples-to-apples comparison between solar, wind, gas, coal, and nuclear.', example: 'Solar LCOE: $30-40/MWh. Onshore wind: $30-50/MWh. New coal: $65-150/MWh. New nuclear: $130-200/MWh. Solar and wind now win on pure economics.' }
