      'In 2007, a house in Las Vegas could sell for $350,000. By 2009, it was worth $120,000. $9 trillion in American household wealth vanished. 10 million people lost their homes. The 2008 financial crisis was the worst economic disaster since the Great Depression, and almost every element was predictable using economic principles. Bubbles follow a pattern, and those who recognize it can protect themselves.',
      'By the end of this lesson, you\'ll understand the anatomy of bubbles, why they form despite rational economics, the mechanisms of financial contagion, and how to recognize bubble warning signs before they pop.',
