      'The 2006 housing market had every bubble warning sign in the textbook. The combination of extreme leverage, deteriorating lending standards, and universal optimism is the definition of the euphoria phase. When the trigger came (adjustable rates reset, prices stopped rising), the leverage amplified losses catastrophically.'
