        'The 2008 crisis demonstrated financial contagion, how a local problem becomes a global catastrophe. Step 1: U.S. homeowners defaulted on subprime mortgages. Step 2: Banks had bundled these mortgages into securities (CDOs) and sold them worldwide. Step 3: When mortgages defaulted, CDO values collapsed, but nobody knew which banks held the toxic assets. Step 4: Banks stopped lending to each other (trust evaporated). Step 5: The credit freeze threatened every business that relied on borrowing.',
        'The speed of contagion was breathtaking. Lehman Brothers filed for bankruptcy on September 15, 2008 (a Monday). By Friday, money market funds were "breaking the buck," AIG needed a $185 billion bailout, and global stock markets had lost $10 trillion. Within weeks, Iceland\'s banking system collapsed, Ireland guaranteed all bank deposits, and the UK nationalized major banks. A local housing bubble in Las Vegas and Miami had crashed the global economy.',
