        { term: 'CDO (Collateralized Debt Obligation)', definition: 'A financial product that bundles multiple loans (often mortgages) into securities sold to investors. Spread mortgage risk globally but also spread the crisis.', example: 'Banks bundled subprime mortgages into CDOs rated AAA (safe). When mortgages defaulted, "safe" CDOs became worthless, destroying $2 trillion in value.' }
