      { takeaway: 'Leverage is the amplifier that turns bubbles into crises', detail: 'Leverage magnifies gains during booms and losses during busts. Zero-down mortgages meant homeowners were wiped out by a 20% price drop. Bank leverage of 30:1 meant a 3% asset loss could cause insolvency. The level of leverage determines the severity of the crash.' },
      { takeaway: 'Five warning signs can help you protect yourself', detail: 'Parabolic price increases, leverage explosion, "this time is different" narratives, widespread amateur participation, and declining quality standards. When multiple signs appear simultaneously, reduce risk, even if timing the exact top is impossible.' }
