        { term: 'Sovereign Wealth Fund', definition: 'A government-owned investment fund that saves resource revenues for future generations and stabilizes the economy during commodity price fluctuations.', example: 'Norway\'s Government Pension Fund: $1.6 trillion, the world\'s largest sovereign wealth fund. Built from oil revenue, it owns 1.5% of all global listed stocks. The model for responsible resource management.' }
